{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-1","title":"Mark 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ followed by multitudes, 3 heals one sick of the palsy; 13 calls Matthew from the receipt of custom; 15 eats with Publicans and sinners; 18 excuses his disciples for not fasting; 23 and for plucking the ears of corn on the sabbath day.</p>\n<p>again. 1:45; Mt 9:1; Lu 5:18 and it. 7:24; Lu 18:35-38; Joh 4:47; Ac 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-2","title":"Mark 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>straightway. 13; 1:33,37,45; 4:1,2; Lu 5:17; 12:1 and he. 1:14; 6:34; Ps 40:9; Mt 5:2; Lu 8:1,11; Ac 8:25; 11:19; 14:25; 16:6 Ro 10:8; 2Ti 4:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-3","title":"Mark 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>bringing. Mt 9:1,2-8; Lu 5:18-26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-4","title":"Mark 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>they uncovered. De 22:8; Lu 5:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-5","title":"Mark 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>saw. Ge 22:12; Joh 2:25; Ac 11:23; 14:9; Eph 2:8; 1Th 1:3,4; Jas 2:18-22 he said. 9,10; Isa 53:11; Mt 9:2; Lu 5:20; 7:47-50; Ac 5:31; 2Co 2:10 Col 3:13 Son.The Jews believed that not only death but all disease was the consequence of sin. \"There is no death without sin, nor any chastisement without iniquity;\" and that \"no diseased person could be healed of his disease till his sins were blotted out.\" Our Lord, therefore, as usual, appeals to their received opinions, and asserts his high dignity, by first forgiving the sins, and then healing the body of the paralytic.</p>\n<p>5:34; Mt 9:22; Lu 8:48 sins. Job 33:17-26; Ps 32:1-5; 90:7-9; 103:3; Isa 38:17; Joh 5:14 1Co 11:30; Jas 5:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-6","title":"Mark 2:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>and reasoning. 8:17; Mt 16:7,8; Lu 5:21,22; 2Co 10:5; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-7","title":"Mark 2:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>speak. 14:64; Mt 9:3; 26:65; Joh 10:33,36 who. Job 14:4; Ps 130:4; Isa 43:25; Da 9:9; Mic 7:18; Lu 5:21; 7:49 Joh 20:20-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-8","title":"Mark 2:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>when. 1Ch 29:17; Mt 9:4; Lu 5:22; 6:8; 7:39,40; Joh 2:24,25; 6:64; 21:17 Heb 4:13; Re 2:23 Why. 7:21; Ps 139:2; Pr 15:26; 24:9; Isa 55:7; Eze 38:10; Lu 24:38; Ac 5:3 Ac 8:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-9","title":"Mark 2:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>is it. Mt 9:5; Lu 5:22-25 Thy sins. 5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-10","title":"Mark 2:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Da 7:13,14; Mt 9:6-8; 16:13; Joh 5:20-27; Ac 5:31; 1Ti 1:13-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-11","title":"Mark 2:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>1:41; Joh 5:8-10; 6:63</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-12","title":"Mark 2:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>insomuch. 1:27; Mt 9:8; 12:23; Lu 7:16 glorified. Mt 15:31; Lu 5:26; 13:13; 17:15; Ac 4:21 We never. Mt 9:33; Joh 7:31; 9:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-13","title":"Mark 2:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>by. Mt 9:9; 13:1 and all. 2; 3:7,8,20,21; 4:1; Pr 1:20-22; Lu 19:48; 21:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-14","title":"Mark 2:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>he saw. 3:18; Mt 9:9; Lu 5:27 Alphaeus. 3:18; Lu 6:15; Ac 1:13 receipt of custom. or, place where the custom was received. Follow me. 1:17-20; Mt 4:19-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-15","title":"Mark 2:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Mt 9:10,11; 21:31,32; Lu 5:29,30; 6:17; 15:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-16","title":"Mark 2:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>How. 7; Isa 65:5; Lu 15:2-7; 18:11; 19:7,10; 1Co 2:15; Heb 12:3 publicans. Mt 18:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-17","title":"Mark 2:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>They that are whole. Mt 9:12,13; Lu 5:31,32; 15:7,29; 16:15; Joh 9:34,40 I came. Isa 1:18; 55:7; Mt 18:11; Lu 15:10; 19:10; Ac 20:21; 26:20 Ro 5:6-8,20,21; 1Co 6:9-11; 1Ti 1:15,16; Tit 2:14; 3:3-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-18","title":"Mark 2:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>the disciples. Mt 9:14-17; Lu 5:33-39 Why. Mt 6:16,18; 23:5; Lu 18:12; Ro 10:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-19","title":"Mark 2:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Can. Ge 29:22; Jud 14:10,11; Ps 45:14; So 6:8; Mt 25:1-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-20","title":"Mark 2:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>the bridegroom. Ps 45:11; So 3:11; Isa 54:5; 62:5; Joh 3:29; 2Co 11:2; Re 19:7; 21:9 be taken. Zec 13:7; Mt 26:31; Joh 7:33,34; 12:8; 13:33; 16:7,28; 17:11,13 Ac 1:9; 3:21 and. Ac 13:2,3; 14:23; 1Co 7:5; 2Co 6:5; 11:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-21","title":"Mark 2:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>seweth. Ps 103:13-15; Isa 57:16; 1Co 10:13 new. or, raw, or, unwrought. Mt 9:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-22","title":"Mark 2:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>bottles. Jos 9:4,13; Job 32:19; Ps 119:80,83; Mt 9:17; Lu 5:37,38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-23","title":"Mark 2:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>that. Mt 12:1-8; Lu 6:1-5 to pluck. De 23:24,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-24","title":"Mark 2:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>why. 7,16; Mt 7:3-5; 15:2,3; 23:23,24; Heb 12:3 that. Ex 20:10; 31:15; 35:2,3; Nu 15:32-36; Ne 13:15-22; Isa 56:2,4,6 Isa 58:13; Jer 17:20-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-25","title":"Mark 2:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Have. 12:20,26; Mt 19:4; 21:16,42; 22:31; Lu 10:26 what. 1Sa 21:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-26","title":"Mark 2:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Abiathar.It appears from the passage referred to here, that Ahimelech was then high priest at Nob; and from other passages, that Abiathar was his son. Various conjectures have been formed in order to solve this difficulty; and some, instead of untying, have cut the knot, by pronouncing it an interpolation. The most probable opinion seems to be, that both father and son had two names, the father being also called Abiathar; and this appears almost certain from 2 Sa 8:17; 1 Ch 18:16, where Ahimelech seems evidently termed Abiathar, while Abiathar is called Ahimelech or Abimelech. (Compare 1 Ki 2:26, 27.)</p>\n<p>1Sa 22:20-22; 23:6,9; 2Sa 8:17; 15:24,29,35; 20:25; 1Ki 1:7 1Ki 2:22,26,27; 4:4 which is not lawful. Ex 29:32,33; Le 24:5-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-27","title":"Mark 2:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>Ex 23:12; De 5:14; Ne 9:13,14; Isa 58:13; Eze 20:12,20; Lu 6:9 Joh 7:23; 1Co 3:21,22; 2Co 4:15; Col 2:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-2-28","title":"Mark 2:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>3:4; Mt 12:8; Lu 6:5; 13:15,16; Joh 5:9-11,17; 9:5-11,14,16 Eph 1:22; Re 1:10</p>"}]}